 },
 "notes": "Audience-first: six top items, Parents, Students, School Life, News, School Calendar, About Us. Home is dropped (the crest links home) and the vague 'Information' section is dissolved, each of its pages going to the audience that owns it. Parents and Students open mega panels of priority-ordered columns plus a featured column of top tasks. Shared tasks (Bell Schedule, Updating Student Contact Information, Grade 7 (Incoming 8) Program Planning, Library) are cross-listed under both audiences. Group headings are only existing page titles that really are parents (PAC, Program Planning, Career Education, Grad 2027, Extra-Curricular, Library Learning Commons). Other clusters (school day, learning, payments and forms, policies) are unheaded columns, because no live copy names them. School Life is a disclosure with no landing page (Drupal route:<button>). It holds the Extra-Curricular and Library hubs and all 8 of their sub-pages that the old menu hid. Audit fixes: every page except the Library Catalogue interstitial is now in the main menu (that one is in the Library hub, and the menu links straight to the catalogue). 'Grad 2026' becomes the page's own title 'Grad 2027' on the year-free alias /students/grad. Library becomes Library Learning Commons, and Career Education & Volunteer Hours becomes Career Education. /students-0 becomes /students. Retired with redirects: /information and /information-0 (to /about-us), the duplicate Back to School post, the empty Research & Inquiry and PAC Constitution and Bylaws pages, and the /media/1069 file page. /information/* pages get aliases under their new owner so Drupal's path-based breadcrumb matches the menu (pathauto plus Redirect). Drupal: the main menu has 3 levels (top item, group head, link). Unheaded groups are runs of level-2 leaves, and menu--main.html.twig starts a new column for each weight band (item.original_link.getWeight() // 10). Cross-listed pages are extra menu_link_content items. No contrib module is needed. Phone: the same tree as an accordion, with each top label a link plus a separate disclosure button. Utility is its own menu block in the header on every page, next to the existing Translate, Search and Accessibility Settings blocks, and becomes the sticky bottom bar on phones. The footer menu has 4 short columns and replaces the duplicated main navigation. Hubs are those nodes in the full_content_with_menu_list_ view mode: sub_pages_menu_block renders the sections as cards, and the bodies are unchanged."
}
